From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8650: let the PCIe GDSCs power off in s2idle

Mainline keeps the SM8650 PCIe GDSCs in retention when they are disabled.
With the controller still powered, the s2idle wake needs a PCIe memory vote
in the sleep set, which keeps DDR and CX from collapsing. Let the GDSCs go
fully off instead: the Wi-Fi (WCN7850) comes back with a fresh PCIe link.
The tablet therefore also skips the PCIe sleep floor (kernel-sm8650 0047).

Taken from https://github.com/enij90/armada-tb321fu (Lenovo Legion Tab Gen 3 / Y700 2025,
TB321FU, SM8650).
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c
@@ -3436,7 +3436,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3447,7 +3447,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3458,7 +3458,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3469,7 +3469,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE | VOTABLE,
 };
 
